; Axis B (cross-ref symbol-slot lookup) — positive direction.
;
; A real `(phrase :name p0)` populates the registry. The `track`
; form omits `:anchor`, which defaults to `p0`. With axis B off,
; the omitted kvpair triggers no lookup at all — clean. With axis
; B on, the overlay-driven lookup resolves `p0` against the
; registered phrase — still clean. Both modes silent.
;
; This fixture documents the axis-on happy path symmetric to
; `effective-axis-b-default-miss`. It produces no harness delta
; today, but serves as a regression guard: a future change that
; makes axis-on spuriously emit on resolved defaults would suddenly
; produce a delta where none exists.
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0"
  (value-kind :name phrase-name
    :underlying symbol
    :cross-ref (cross-ref :target phrase))
  (form :name phrase
    (key :name name :type symbol :optional false))
  (form :name track
    (key :name anchor :type phrase-name :default p0 :optional true)))

(phrase :name p0)
(track)
